[
  {
    "id": "sitl40-tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "SITL 40 Transition events",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "Fly ArduPilot sysid 1 and watch the flight-dynamic transition events land in a State feed: mode-changed on GUIDED, armed-changed on arm, home-changed when the EKF sets home, landed-changed on takeoff (EXTENDED_SYS_STATE is streamed explicitly — this SITL does not send it unasked).",
    "env": []
  },
  {
    "id": "sitl40-comment",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "sitl40-tab",
    "name": "Flight-dynamic transition events",
    "info": "Chain: GUIDED (confirm) → 2 s settle → Arm (confirm) → SET_MESSAGE_INTERVAL for EXTENDED_SYS_STATE (245) at 2 Hz → Takeoff 10 m (complete).\n\nGUIDED ACK is not armable-yet: ARM in the same tick returns FAILED (4) on Copter-4.7.0; a short delay lets the mode apply. Prep leaves STABILIZE so Set GUIDED is a real mode-changed edge.\n\nThe State feed subscribes to only the six transition events — armed-changed, mode-changed, landed-changed, gps-fix-changed, home-changed, sensor-health-changed — so the debug pane shows edges, not traffic. Each record carries sysid/compid plus from/to (sensor-health-changed adds the flipped-bit mask as changed).\n\nFirst observation is not a transition: the feed stays quiet until a held value actually changes, so expect nothing at connect and a burst around mode/arm/takeoff.\n\nConnection: bind 0.0.0.0:14550 → remote 127.0.0.1:14551, sysid 1.",
    "x": 250,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
